# Strahd's letters (docs/regions/strahd_presence.md; data/strahd/visits.json): the first letter, brought by a Vistani
# rider from the third day, and the dinner invitation with the black carriage once the party is level 9. Getting in
# sets strahd_invitation = "accepted"; the visit's `then` takes the party to the castle's front door.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The first letter

~ first
set strahd_letter_read
Narrator: A rider in Vistani colours reins in beside you, holds out a letter sealed in black wax, and is gone back up the road before anyone can ask who sent it.
Narrator: The seal is one letter, a Z, pressed deep.
Strahd: My dear guests. Forgive a host for writing when he might call. The daylight is so inconvenient for me.
if flag.strahd_watcher_seen
Strahd: You saw me on the ridge. You looked well. A little thin. Do eat.
endif
if flag.death_house_completed
Strahd: You found your way out of the house on the hill. Most do not. I have the house to thank for introducing us.
endif
if guest:ireena
Strahd: You have Ireena with you. Keep her warm and keep her close. I should be desolate if anything happened to her that I had not arranged.
elif flag.ireena_sanctuary == "st_andrals"
Strahd: You have left Ireena with a priest and his saint. How touching. Saints are so rarely at home.
elif flag.ireena_sanctuary == "inn" or flag.ireena_in_krezk
Strahd: You have put Ireena behind a wall and a door. I have always admired walls. They tell me exactly where to look.
endif
if tarokka.drawn
Strahd: The old woman at the pool has told you a story about me. She tells it to everyone. It always ends the same way.
endif
Strahd: Go where you like. See what my land has to show you. When you are ready, we will dine. Until then I remain your host, Strahd von Zarovich.
* Burn it. -> first_burned
* Keep it. -> first_kept

~ first_burned
Narrator: The paper takes the flame slowly, as if it would rather not, and the black wax runs like something alive.
-> END

~ first_kept
set strahd_letter_kept
Narrator: You fold it away. For a while it is warm against you. Then, oddly, it isn't.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The invitation and the black carriage (level 9)

~ invitation
if flag.strahd_invitation == "declined"
Narrator: The black carriage again, waiting on the road with its door open, as patient as a stone.
else
Narrator: A black carriage waits on the road ahead, drawn by two black horses with embers for eyes. It has no driver. Its door stands open.
endif
Narrator: On the seat lies a letter sealed in black wax.
Strahd: My guests. You have grown remarkable, and I have grown curious. Dine with me tonight at Castle Ravenloft. The carriage knows the way.
if flag.strahd_letter_kept
Strahd: You kept my first letter. I noticed. I notice everything that concerns you.
endif
if flag.strahd_night_visit == "attacked"
Strahd: Bring your weapons, by all means. I forgive the business by your fire. A host must.
endif
if flag.strahd_test == "fought"
Strahd: You fought well on my road. Come and let me thank you properly.
endif
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena is welcome, of course. Her room has been ready for a very long time.
Ireena [angry]: I'll ride in his coach when I'm dead. Which is what he's hoping.
endif
Strahd: No harm will come to you under my roof before the meal is over. You have my word, and my word is older than your kingdoms.
* Get in. -> accept
* Not tonight. -> decline
* Tear up the letter. -> tear

~ accept
set strahd_invitation = "accepted"
Narrator: The door shuts behind you on its own. The carriage moves off with no word and no whip, faster than horses should, up into the mountains and the cloud.
time +90
-> END

~ decline
set strahd_invitation = "declined"
Narrator: The door swings shut. The carriage turns in the road with great care and goes back the way it came.
-> END

~ tear
set strahd_invitation = "declined"
Narrator: The pieces go off in the wind. The horses watch you do it. Then the carriage turns and goes, unhurried, like something that will be back.
-> END
